# Introducing [Newsy]($link.url("https://newsy.lightcms.me").new(true)): A Newsletter Platform Powered by GitHub

[Newsy]($link.url("https://newsy.lightcms.me").new(true)) is a newsletter platform inspired by projects like [Utterances]($link.url("https://utteranc.es").new(true)), [Giscus]($link.url("https://giscus.app").new(true)), and [Gitalk]($link.url("https://gitalk.github.io").new(true))  projects that reimagined commenting on static sites by using GitHub Issues as the backend.

Newsy takes the same idea and applies it to newsletters.

Instead of relying on a traditional email marketing service, maintaining a separate mailing list, or paying for SMTP APIs, your newsletter can live alongside your code in a GitHub repository.

[Newsy]($link.url("https://newsy.lightcms.me").new(true)) is built around a simple idea: creating a newsletter should never be a complicated expensive thing.

It aims to remove much of the overhead that comes with traditional newsletter platforms while keeping everything close to the tools developers already use.

